# Infiny OS lives in its own repository. The Box and the OS are different
# products with different promises — the Box is a container with no screen,
# the OS is a system with a desktop. Keeping both here would ship people code
# that cannot work in the Box and was never meant to.

# Benchmark harness and its raw data. Research tooling, not product: it never
# enters the image and nobody who downloads the Box needs it.
scripts/
bin/

# Internal working documents: decision history, machine-specific details,
# the Phase 2 build guide. Readers need README, not these.
CONTEXT.md
GUIDE.md
PHASE1.md

# Environment and build artifacts
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
infiny.wsl
infiny-rootfs.tar
infiny.raw
infiny.qcow2

# Local state
.claude/
*.log

# Secrets. None belong here in the first place; these rules exist for the
# "put it there for a minute and forgot" case, which is the case that happens.
key.txt
pass.txt
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
secrets.*

# Release archives. Half a gigabyte in history makes a repository nobody
# clones — these belong in GitHub Releases, attached to a tag.
dist/
*.zip
